# width: 120
# height: 40
# The palette box is anchored on the frame it opened on. Its height comes
# from the filtered count and `overlay.place` re-centres what it is given,
# so re-placing it every frame slid the whole box DOWN the screen as the
# list shrank under the query — the reader's eye chased a moving box while
# typing. Only the list shrinks now (VS Code's palette does the same).
#
# The activity-bar margin differs per row, so the row the top border sits
# on is identifiable: it opens on a blank-margin row, and before this it
# had moved onto the row whose margin carries the 󰎒 glyph.
write a.txt hello
open a.txt
command palette
expect screen contains "   │           ┌ Command palette "
type toggle wrap
expect screen contains "toggle wrap"
expect screen contains "   │           ┌ Command palette "
key esc
